SUMMARY
One of our system administrators identified a large number of Audit Failure events in the Windows Security Event log.

SOURCE
https://blueteamlabs.online/home/challenge/bruteforce-16629bf9a2

STEPS TAKEN
Question 1) How many Audit Failure events are there? (Format: Count of Events)
I imported the .txt file into Kali and ran a grep:
grep "Audit Failure" [file] | wc -l
Answer: 3103

Question 2) What is the username of the local account that is being targeted? (Format: Username)
For this one, I just opened the file itself. There are some successes close to the bottom, but just before that - showing several failures - is for the account "administrator."

Question 3) What is the failure reason related to the Audit Failure logs?
This one is towards the top of the log file: Unknown user name or bad password.

Question 4) What is the Windows Event ID associated with these logon failures?
This is open source intelligence - 4625.

Question 5) What is the source IP conducting this attack?
Also towards the top: 113.161.192.227

Question 6) What country is this IP address associated with?
User ICANN lookup:
Mailing Address: Ha Noi, VietNam

Question 7) What is the range of source ports that were used by the attacker to make these login requests? (LowestPort-HighestPort - Ex: 100-541)
Grepping, filtering the unique values, and sorting them in order will tell you this information:
grep "Source Port" '/home/jessi/Projects/BTLO_Bruteforce_Challenge.txt' | uniq | sort
The bottom one that you see first will be the last value, and to easily find the first, add "| head".
Answer: 49162 - 65534
